NNAAMMEE
     ggrroouuppiinnffoo — display group information

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ggrroouuppiinnffoo [--ee] _g_r_o_u_p

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ggrroouuppiinnffoo utility displays the name, group ID (GID), and members of
     the specified _g_r_o_u_p.

     The options are as follows:

     --ee      Do not display anything (quiet mode).  This form of the command
             is useful for scripts which need to check whether a particular
             group name or GID is already in use on the system.

     The _g_r_o_u_p argument may be either a group name or a GID.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The ggrroouuppiinnffoo utility exits 0 if _g_r_o_u_p exists, and non-zero if it does
     not.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     group(5), passwd(5), group(8), userinfo(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ggrroouuppiinnffoo utility first appeared in OpenBSD 2.7.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The ggrroouuppiinnffoo utility was written by Alistair G. Crooks <_a_g_c_@_N_e_t_B_S_D_._o_r_g>.

CCAAVVEEAATTSS
     If the specified _g_r_o_u_p is the primary group of a user, but that user is
     not listed as a member of the _g_r_o_u_p in the group(5) file, the ggrroouuppiinnffoo
     utility fails to list that user as a member of the _g_r_o_u_p.

